            <ArticleTitle>[Studies on the analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect of bornyl acetate in volatile oil from Amomum villosum].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>438-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To study analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects of bornyl acetate, the main ingredient of Amomum villosum volatile oil.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The analgesic effects were tested by hot-plate and writhing reaction method, the ear swelling caused by dimethylbenzene in mice.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Bornyl acetate could restrain writhing reaction caused by acetic acid glacial, lighten the pain caused by hot-plate. It could also suppress ear swelling caused by dimethylbenzene in mice.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Bornyl acetate shows analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
